indications_limitations:
&lt;p&gt; Laboratory tests are essential to monitor the progress of CRD patients. The following list and frequencies of tests constitute the level and types of routine laboratory tests that are covered. Bills for other types of tests are considered nonroutine. Routine tests at greater frequencies must include medical justification. Nonroutine tests generally are justified by the diagnosis.  The routinely covered regimen includes the following tests.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Per Dialysis &lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; All hematocrit or hemoglobin and clotting time tests furnished incident to dialysis treatments.&lt;&sol;li&gt;&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Per Week &lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; Prothrombin time for patients on anticoagulant therapy&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; Serum Creatinine&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Per Week or Thirteen Per Quarter &lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; BUN&lt;&sol;li&gt;&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Monthly &lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt; 
&lt;li&gt; CBC&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Serum Calcium&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Serum Potassium&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Serum Chloride&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Serum Bicarbonate&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Serum Phosphorous&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Total Protein&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Serum Albumin&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Alkaline Phospatase&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; AST, SGOT&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; LDH&lt;&sol;li&gt;&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Guidelines for tests other than those routinely performed include:&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt; 
&lt;li&gt; Serum Aluminum - one every 3 months&lt;&sol;li&gt;

&lt;li&gt; Serum Ferritin - one every 3 months&lt;&sol;li&gt;
&lt;&sol;ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The following tests for hepatitis B are covered when patients first enter a dialysis facility: Hepatitis B surface antigen (HBsAg), Anti-HBs.  Coverage of future testing in these patients depends on their serologic status and on whether they have been successfully immunized against hepatitis B virus. The following table summarizes the frequency of serologic surveillance for hepatitis B. Tests furnished according to this table do not require additional documentation and are paid separately because payment for maintenance dialysis treatments does not take them into account.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
